[{:seon.task/name "an-import-from-a-checkout-behind-main-deletes-nothing-main-added"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by tests2, 2026-11-17: session/tests2's seon_done merged 1da645f6e7, which deleted flow's seon.prove-test/a-branch-that-moved-a-build-input-gets-a-candidate-built-from-it (landed by 0a4c4b9393 a few minutes before). The agent's judge had merged main into the branch (seon.agent/judge!, merge-main!), then the session imported test/seon/prove_test.clj from its worktree, which was behind main: my.branch/import! reads the file whole and writes it as the branch's text, so every form main added since the worktree's base reads as one the branch removed, and the merge into main carries the removal. A git three-way merge of the worktree's commit with main kept it (checked: the other nine files of the merge matched git's merge exactly). Fix at the cause: import! diffs the checkout's file against the checkout's own base (the git merge base with main, or the commit the branch last imported from), never against the branch's text, so it writes only what the session changed; a form the checkout lacks that its base also lacks is main's, kept. Proof, red first on today's import!: a branch holding main's new deftest, an import of the file from a checkout whose base predates it, and the deftest still on the branch."
